From 4dec40e4416c0a05f460bca0a9f8b61042ee29c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:32:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge, settings: the black of the display for
 pictures mapped to it as HDR10

The black of the display was taken into account for Dolby Vision Low-Latency
only. "Black of the display" (expert level, 0 to 0.5 cd/m2, 0 by default)
does the same for "Adapt Dolby Vision to my display (projectors)" and, while
that is on, for "HDR10 and HDR10+ adapted to the display": the black level lift
of ITU-R BT.2390 (5.4.1) on the mapped picture in PQ, after libplacebo's
mapping, as Low-Latency has it, so that what is just above black does not sink
into the display's own black. With 0 the shader of the output is the one
before, its text and its signature: the same bytes.

Measured on Mesa's software OpenGL ES (llvmpipe and zink), content that the
display holds: within 0.032 of a 12-bit PQ code of the lift computed exactly,
the black of the source at the display's black (0.05 and 0.0005 cd/m2), and
the right shader when the mapping changes on a renderer that is kept, as it
is from one video to the next.
